# Line endings
#
# This repository is developed on Windows but the product is a Linux app, and two
# files decide whether it installs at all: install.sh and crimsonx.desktop. If git
# checks them out as CRLF, Linux fails with "bad interpreter" / "$'\r': command not
# found". Pin them, regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.desktop text eol=lf

# Binary assets - never convert, never diff
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.dat binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
